  "answer": "The assistant should correct the sales note. Official policy is the source of truth: sales transcripts or playbooks may informally claim “immediately on request,” but the Security and Data Governance Policy is the sole authority for deletion timelines, and standard deletion is executed within 90 days after contract termination [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. Under that standard process, data is immediately removed from active access, but physical deletion of database records and document chunks from primary storage and backups takes up to 90 days [NL-019#NL-019-S05]. The sales playbook itself warns against promising immediate deletion without consulting Security/Legal and confirms it is a lower-authority resource [NL-009#NL-009-S08]. A faster custom SLA can be offered to Enterprise clients only if explicitly documented in a signed DPA and configured by engineering [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. So the assistant should explain the 90-day standard timeline, not confirm immediate deletion, and offer to formalize any custom deletion SLA in the DPA.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer  \nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
